  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 12 actions (actions.js, getActions) and 9 boolean feedbacks (feedbacks.js, getFeedbacks); both are built in one pass with no runtime-generated entries. Variables (variables.js) are not catalogued.",
    "Protocol: TelnetHelper to the configured host on fixed port 23 (index.js initTCP), commands are sent with a trailing \"\\n\". SIS escape commands are used for recording (\"<ESC>Y<n>RCDR\"), extend (\"<ESC>E<min>RCDR\"), RTMP (\"<ESC>E<stream>*<0|1>RTMP\"), chapter marker (\"<ESC>BRCDR\") and audio mute (\"<ESC>M<type>000<channel>*<0|1>AU\"); presets use \"<type>*....\" strings with the type numbers from PRESET in index.js.",
    "All dropdowns are closed lists defined as class fields in index.js (CHANNEL, RECORD, ENCODER, ONOFF, AUDIOINCHANNEL, AUDIOOUTCHANNEL, AUDIOTYPE, MUTEUNMUTE). Choice ids are strings. Several feedback defaults are numbers (record_bg default 1, onoff default 0) while the choice ids are strings, as written in the source; the callbacks compare with parseInt(), so both spellings work at runtime.",
    "The number fields also carry range: false in the source (a field that is not part of the catalog schema); it is not recorded. Number fields have no asInteger.",
    "The audio_mute feedback compares the stored state with feedback.options.mute as a string, unlike the other feedbacks which use parseInt.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.10.0: options do not support expressions."
  ]
}
